From d61e0b4e0626854f232c2fa3a29b05fc2547bc75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pete O_o <pmb@meta.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 14:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Event: carry the CPER section onto the pushed EventRecord

Patch 0410 renders CPER on the Redfish LogEntry resource, but the realtime
Event pushed to EventDestination subscribers never carried it, so a
subscriber had no way to see a CPER without following LogEntry.@odata.id and
issuing a second GET.

The data was already present and being discarded. A log entry's
InterfacesAdded signal carries every interface the entry exposes, but
onDbusEventLogCreated() forwarded only the property map of
xyz.openbmc_project.Logging.Entry -- so
xyz.openbmc_project.Logging.Extension.CPER.Processed, which holds
DiagnosticDataType/NotificationType/SectionType/Oem, was dropped before
anything could read it.

Collect that interface's property map alongside the Entry's, carry it on
EventLogObjectsType, and merge it into the record in formatEventLogEntry().
The Redfish shape is produced by fillEventLogCperFromPropertyMap(), the same
helper 0410 uses for the LogEntry resource, so the two representations cannot
drift. CPER is the identical schema object on both.

Two deliberate choices:

- The raw-CPER cross-link is not requested. Links.RelatedLogEntries is a
  LogEntry construct with no counterpart on EventRecord, so the hasRawCper
  argument is left at its default of false.

- The pushed payload moves from #Event.v1_7_0.Event to #Event.v1_8_0.Event.
  v1_8_0 is the first revision in which EventRecord defines CPER,
  DiagnosticData and DiagnosticDataType; emitting them under v1_7_0 would be
  schema-invalid. Note the installed CSDL/JSON schema pack may need
  regenerating to match, the same consideration 0410 raised when it moved
  LogEntry from v1_9_0 to v1_15_0.

Entries with no CPER extension are byte-identical to before: the carrier is
empty and the merge loop does nothing.

Tests: dbus_log_watcher_test gains a case asserting the CPER extension is
carried through with the vendor blob re-parsed into a real object, that an
empty SectionType is omitted rather than emitted blank, and that no Links
member appears on the record. The two existing cases now assert the
no-CPER path leaves the record untouched.
